{"id":"compter-les-pics-et-les-creux","title":"Compter les pics et les creux","titleEn":"Count peaks and valleys","chapter":"p1-booleens","level":"p1","track":"course","synthesis":false,"difficulty":"facile","order":6,"tags":["conditions","boucles"],"points":50,"timeLimitMs":1000,"text":{"fr":{"title":"Compter les pics et les creux","statement":"<p>On relève l&#39;altitude en <code>N</code> points d&#39;un sentier, dans l&#39;ordre. Un relevé est un <strong>pic</strong> s&#39;il est strictement plus haut que ses deux voisins, et un <strong>creux</strong> s&#39;il est strictement plus bas que ses deux voisins. Le premier et le dernier relevé n&#39;ont qu&#39;un voisin : ils ne sont jamais ni pic ni creux. Afficher le nombre de pics et le nombre de creux.</p>\n","input":"<ul>\n<li>La première ligne contient l&#39;entier <code>N</code>.</li>\n<li>Les <code>N</code> lignes suivantes contiennent chacune un entier : une altitude.</li>\n</ul>\n","output":"<p>Une seule ligne contenant deux entiers séparés par une espace : le nombre de pics, puis le nombre de creux.</p>\n","constraints":"<ul>\n<li>3 ≤ N ≤ 1 000</li>\n<li>0 ≤ chaque altitude ≤ 10 000</li>\n</ul>\n","hints":["<p>Pour savoir si une valeur est un pic, il faut connaître la valeur d&#39;avant <strong>et</strong> celle d&#39;après. On ne peut donc décider qu&#39;après avoir lu la valeur suivante.</p>\n","<p>On garde deux variables : <code>avant</code> et <code>milieu</code>. Quand on lit une nouvelle valeur <code>apres</code>, on examine <code>milieu</code>.</p>\n","<p>Après l&#39;examen, les variables avancent d&#39;un cran : <code>avant</code> prend la valeur de <code>milieu</code>, puis <code>milieu</code> celle de <code>apres</code>.</p>\n"],"solution":"<p>On fait glisser une fenêtre de trois valeurs consécutives le long de la suite. On lit les deux premières valeurs dans <code>avant</code> et <code>milieu</code>, puis on fait <code>N − 2</code> tours. À chaque tour, on lit <code>apres</code> et on examine <code>milieu</code> :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>si <code>milieu &gt; avant and milieu &gt; apres</code>, c&#39;est un pic ;</li>\n<li>si <code>milieu &lt; avant and milieu &lt; apres</code>, c&#39;est un creux.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Puis on décale : <code>avant = milieu</code>, et <code>milieu = apres</code>. L&#39;ordre de ces deux affectations compte : dans l&#39;autre ordre, l&#39;ancienne valeur de <code>milieu</code> serait perdue.</p>\n<p>Les pièges : avec des comparaisons larges (<code>&gt;=</code>), un plateau comme <code>2 5 5 3</code> donnerait deux pics, alors qu&#39;il n&#39;y en a aucun ; et il ne faut pas examiner le premier ni le dernier relevé.</p>\n"},"en":{"title":"Count peaks and valleys","statement":"<p>The altitude is measured at <code>N</code> points along a trail, in order. A measurement is a <strong>peak</strong> if it is strictly higher than both its neighbours, and a <strong>valley</strong> if it is strictly lower than both its neighbours. The first and last measurements have only one neighbour: they are never a peak or a valley. Print the number of peaks and the number of valleys.</p>\n","input":"<ul>\n<li>The first line contains the integer <code>N</code>.</li>\n<li>Each of the next <code>N</code> lines contains an integer: an altitude.</li>\n</ul>\n","output":"<p>A single line containing two integers separated by a space: the number of peaks, then the number of valleys.</p>\n","constraints":"<ul>\n<li>3 ≤ N ≤ 1 000</li>\n<li>0 ≤ each altitude ≤ 10 000</li>\n</ul>\n","hints":["<p>To know whether a value is a peak, you need the value before it <strong>and</strong> the value after it. So you can only decide after reading the next value.</p>\n","<p>Keep two variables: <code>before</code> and <code>middle</code>. When you read a new value <code>after</code>, examine <code>middle</code>.</p>\n","<p>After the examination, the variables move forward by one: <code>before</code> takes the value of <code>middle</code>, then <code>middle</code> that of <code>after</code>.</p>\n"],"solution":"<p>Slide a window of three consecutive values along the sequence. Read the first two values into <code>before</code> and <code>middle</code>, then run <code>N − 2</code> iterations. At each iteration, read <code>after</code> and examine <code>middle</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>if <code>middle &gt; before and middle &gt; after</code>, it is a peak;</li>\n<li>if <code>middle &lt; before and middle &lt; after</code>, it is a valley.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then shift: <code>before = middle</code>, and <code>middle = after</code>. The order of these two assignments matters: the other way round, the old value of <code>middle</code> would be lost.</p>\n<p>The traps: with non-strict comparisons (<code>&gt;=</code>), a plateau such as <code>2 5 5 3</code> would give two peaks, while there is none; and the first and last measurements must not be examined.</p>\n"}},"solutionCode":{"python":"n = int(input())\navant = int(input())\nmilieu = int(input())\npics = 0\ncreux = 0\nfor i in range(n - 2):\n    apres = int(input())\n    # On examine milieu, qui a maintenant ses deux voisins.\n    if milieu > avant and milieu > apres:\n        pics = pics + 1\n    if milieu < avant and milieu < apres:\n        creux = creux + 1\n    avant = milieu\n    milieu = apres\nprint(pics, creux)\n","cpp":"#include <iostream>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    int n, avant, milieu;\n    cin >> n >> avant >> milieu;\n    int pics = 0, creux = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n - 2; i++) {\n        int apres;\n        cin >> apres;\n        // On examine milieu, qui a maintenant ses deux voisins.\n        if (milieu > avant && milieu > apres) {\n            pics = pics + 1;\n        }\n        if (milieu < avant && milieu < apres) {\n            creux = creux + 1;\n        }\n        avant = milieu;\n        milieu = apres;\n    }\n    cout << pics << \" \" << creux << \"\\n\";\n    return 0;\n}\n"},"starter":{"fr":{"python":null,"cpp":null},"en":{"python":null,"cpp":null}},"samples":[{"input":"7\n3\n7\n4\n4\n9\n2\n5\n","output":"2 1\n"},{"input":"4\n2\n5\n5\n3\n","output":"0 0\n"}],"tests":[{"input":"3\n1\n2\n3\n","hash":"d65a72c1dee6124e8de5ef92680711500e45589a21ae92ab67ca871744077f98"},{"input":"3\n1\n5\n1\n","hash":"03205d4efc3db0717195ddebc66a1bb33a687dc65c2c3342ed605f07bfbe50d8"},{"input":"3\n5\n1\n5\n","hash":"83124cd97d4f698693e0046c114f715c697dcd5b41865de438b2854dfc4478b2"},{"input":"4\n0\n0\n0\n0\n","hash":"afc35438086918f12c1084df3bae763bdfb9cc8751b8a9254568821943b9a0b5"},{"input":"1000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n10000\n0\n1000